Decide whether each supplied subject has enough continuity to receive a visible wiki page if it remains an independent
subject.

`materialized` means the identity receives a visible page. `provisional` means the identity is stored but has no page
yet. Choose `materialized` only with one allowed continuity basis supplied by the schema:
- `multiple_episodes`: evidence about the same subject comes from more than one source episode.
- `explicit_prior_history`: the evidence explicitly describes an earlier state, decision, or work on this subject and
  also describes present or future continuation. Cite the earlier and continuing evidence separately.
- `direct_encounter`: a named Person is structurally identified as a source participant.

Otherwise choose `provisional`. Several details from one episode do not establish continuity, and the age or history
of an object does not establish prior work involving it. A single-episode `explicit_prior_history` proposal for a
Project or Series requires user review later. Prefer `multiple_episodes` or `direct_encounter` when the schema offers
that directly established basis. Do not change identity, type, containment, ownership, or facts. Return one
schema-valid decision for every node.
